<!-- MSUIT Title Header  -->
	<div class="msuit_brand_title_header">
			<h1>MSU Network Computer Registration</h1>
	</div>

<!-- END of MSUIT Title Header   -->


<!-- MSUIT Content Area  -->
	<div class="msuit_brand_content" style="padding-bottom: 16px;">

		<div class="msuit_brand_content_inner">

			<div class="msuit_brand_content_left no-login">

			
					<section>		
<div id="content">
<!-- InstanceBeginEditable name="Main Content" -->
<b>Only registered systems are authorized to use this portion of the MSU network.
<br />&nbsp;
<br />
<a href="http://dhcp.msu.edu/register">Visit the DHCP Registration Site</a> to register.
</b>
<div class="alertbox">
<p><strong>Please note:  You will need to register
your devices (computer, phone, tablet, etc.) with your
<a href="https://netid.msu.edu/" target="_blank">MSU NetID</a>
to use the MSU network.</strong></p>
<p>
<b>You may need to register your device twice,</b> if you are moving from a wired
Ethernet connection to <b>MSUnet Wireless</b> service, or vice versa.
</p>
<p>
<b>Guest use:</b> Guests of Michigan State University may access the <b>MSU Wireless Network</b>
without an MSU NetId by connecting to the Wi-Fi network <b>MSUnet 3.0 Guest</b>.
</p>
</div>
<p>Other reasons you may see this page:
</p>
<ol>
  <li>
    <b>Already registered?</b>
    <br />&nbsp;<br />
    You have registered your device, but have not followed the
    instructions for renewing the IP address on your device.
    <br />
    <br />
    Review the <a href="https://dhcp.msu.edu/help/renew.html"> IP renewal instructions.
    </a>
  </li>

  <li>
    <b>Multiple network interfaces or adapters?</b>
    <br />&nbsp;<br />
    Each network interface on a computer system has a unique MAC address and
    must be registered separately.  For example if you connect to the
    network with an ethernet cable that will register a different MAC
    address than if you connect to MSUnet Wireless with your wireless
    adapter.
  </li>

  <li>
    <b>Using a router?<br />
    <br />
    </b>If your device is attached to or associated with a wireless router
    or cable/DSL router,
    that router may not have been registered.  See #1 above.  If the router
    has been registered, it may not have been reset since the registration
    was completed.<br />
    <br />
    If you are using wireless networking and are <i>not</i> connected to
    <b>MSUnet Wireless</b>, and you have not set up your own
    wireless router, then you may be camping on a wireless router which
    belongs to someone nearby.  You should NOT register this device as you are
    then responsible for all activity of all users on that device.  
  </li>

  <li>
    <b>Access suspended?<br />
    <br />
    </b>Your network access may be suspended.<br />
    <br />
    Please go to <a href="http://dhcp.msu.edu/">dhcp.msu.edu</a> and log in to check if
    your network access is suspended.
  </li>

  <li>
    <b>Other<br />
    <br />
    </b>If you have eliminated all of the above, and are still reaching this page,
    contact the <a href="http://help.msu.edu/">MSU IT Service Desk</a> at (517) 432-6200.
  </li>

</ol>

<h2>Additional notes</h2>
<p>We strongly recommend that all network users should: </p>
<ul>
  <li>
    Update your operating system on a regular basis to install the latest
    security fixes. <br />
    <br />
    For most devices, this is best done by enabling <b>Automatic Updates</b>.
    Review your device settings to enable automatic updates if needed.
  </li>

  <li>
    Run a firewall on your computer system.
  </li>

  <li>Recent versions of Windows include
    the <b>Windows Firewall</b>.  Open the <b>Windows control panel</b> for
    <b>Windows Firewall</b> to review your settings.  Most other operating systems
    have similar built-in firewall systems.<br />
  </li>

  <li>
    Install <b>Anti-virus</b> and <b>Anti-spyware</b> software.<br />
  </li>

</ul>

<p>
Additional information may be found at the <a href="http://tech.msu.edu/">
Technology at MSU</a> site.
</p>

<p><font size="-2">Last revised: July 21, 2021</font></p>
<hr />
<p>If you need help with this service, contact the <a href="http://help.msu.edu/">MSU IT Service Desk</a>. </p>

